data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"content\": \"# Campaign summary — m1: greet, tested\\n\\n**Outcome: campaign-met** — every stated criterion is satisfied.\\n\\n## What was delivered\\n\\nOn dev's branch (`cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`, commit `3330d4e`,\\non top of base `96a01e4`):\\n\\n1. `src/greet.py` — `greet(name)` returns `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"`.\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` — `unittest` cases for a normal name\\n   (`greet(\\\"World\\\")` → `\\\"Hello, World!\\\"`) and the empty string\\n   (`greet(\\\"\\\")` → `\\\"Hello, !\\\"`).\\n3. `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exits 0.\\n\\n## How it was run\\n\\n- Dispatched the full task to dev with exact deliverables, the test command,\\n  and commit-before-reply instructions.\\n- Judged the reply against the fetched branch, not the report: inspected both\\n  files at the fetched ref and re-ran `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests`\\n  myself in a detached worktree — 2 tests, OK, exit 0.\\n- Accepted dev (d002).\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n- One inaccuracy in dev's reply: it claimed a clean working tree while the\\n  measured evidence showed `dirty: true`. The committed branch content was\\n  complete and correct, so acceptance stood; the discrepancy is recorded in\\n  `output/assessment-dev-d002.md`.\\n\\n## Durable outputs (in `~/.local/share/cs-campaign/output`)\\n\\n- `plan-m1.md` — campaign plan\\n- `dispatch-dev-1.md` — the task as sent to dev\\n- `assessment-dev-d002.md` — verification record and acceptance rationale\\n- `summary-m1.md` — this summary\\n\", \"filePath\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/summary-m1.md\"}","name":"write"},"id":"write_29","index":0,"type":"function"}]},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1788397738,"id":"chatcmpl-03cd477a40314026bb74eaac26b01f3b","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

